 "Quipus (khipus) are assemblages of coloured, spun and knotted cords used by Andean societies—especially the Inca—to record numerical and possibly narrative information. Spanish officials described specialist quipucamayocs. Surviving quipus encode decimal place values in knot types and positions. Whether some quipus also encode phonetic or narrative data remains an active research question.",
